  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Swertisin and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, as Swertisin is identified as a target of multiple compounds that are themselves targets of the complex. Specifically, Swertisin is linked to WI-38 cells, which are known to be targets of several compounds, including (Z,Z)-1,3,11-Tridecatriene-5,7,9-triyne, 1-Vinyl-8-Hydroxy-Beta-Carboline, and 2-[(1R)-1-(4-hydroxyphenyl)prop-2-enyl]-5-methoxycyclohexa-2,5-diene-1,4-dione. These compounds are all known to interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, indicating a possible pathway through which Swertisin may influence the complex's activity. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a strong, possibly direct, interaction between Swertisin and the complex, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a plausible biological connection, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the functional role of Swertisin in this context.",
